 *
 * Here "core" must run before "ui", and both before "app", so the order is
 * [core, ui, app].
 *
 * Rules -- all of them are checked:
 *  - A name that only ever appears inside a prerequisite list is still a task, with no
 *    prerequisites of its own. So {"b": ["a"]} has two tasks and the order is [a, b].
 *  - Many orders are usually legal, so the tie-break is fixed: whenever more than one
 *    task is ready (all of its prerequisites already placed), take the one that is
 *    alphabetically smallest. That makes exactly one answer correct.
 *  - A null or empty map gives an empty list.
 *  - A duplicate prerequisite ("b": ["a", "a"]) is harmless and means the same as listing
 *    it once. A null prerequisite list means the same as an empty one.
 *  - If the prerequisites contain a cycle -- including a task that lists itself -- throw
 *    IllegalStateException. Do not return a partial order.
